#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064220 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064092 :question/id #uuid "cb771ff3-b5a9-5900-913f-df23957760b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-472" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt 2} \\dfrac{1}{2+x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+{x}^{2}/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this integral now resembles the basic integral for the inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\,\\textrm d u = \\arctan{u} + C.\n$$\n\nWe make the substitution $u=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt 2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\sqrt 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332 :topic/math-academy-id 1159 :topic/title "Calculating Definite Integrals Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "400b63a0-4683-5a21-897e-9f816d13ecf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285387} {:answer/id #uuid "72dc0745-c711-5555-b758-8857ea08db0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285845} {:answer/id #uuid "7e97b556-fb4d-50ab-8db3-611fbf05e7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285953} {:answer/id #uuid "85326801-a074-5ff0-bebe-99064aa9feb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286012} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f53bfe-9dac-5f4c-b151-f462bed9f133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72dc0745-c711-5555-b758-8857ea08db0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285845} :answer-field/id #uuid "a839d901-bb07-5422-9156-0f0bc9d6308d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287488}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa336cf9-b3b8-5d4a-a543-f9cee172da34" :question/math-academy-id "q-19394" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/2)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3caebccd-a111-5c41-885b-601d0e3537ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285359} {:answer/id #uuid "5c49b8ca-6a4c-5d5b-bee0-678ddd9d003c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285633} {:answer/id #uuid "77e0a940-8e6f-54a7-9506-301d4949f5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285904} {:answer/id #uuid "c96c9e76-bbaf-5ac6-a64e-a08681842df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286625} {:answer/id #uuid "eda35d92-71e9-5870-9644-e45103f5e6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c96c9e76-bbaf-5ac6-a64e-a08681842df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286625} :answer-field/id #uuid "23ae6c57-6433-571b-8f19-8245bed72d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287223}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4167c2cd-a204-5a1b-9ee4-1fca54336ae6" :question/math-academy-id "q-19397" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2+8{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2+8{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $14$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2+8{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{1+(2x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{14}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{14}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)-\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "243323f6-ad70-573c-a08a-406469d3a0ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247740} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7538ae-df96-5bd6-89c4-eb9b39dfc0b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247852} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf8e15f-3174-57fb-b8e4-5d360ff846f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248257} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8775a6-08c9-5e68-8ded-0ebea2805076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248846} {:answer/id #uuid "a3358706-6bfa-540b-8aac-27669d842b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bf8e15f-3174-57fb-b8e4-5d360ff846f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248257} :answer-field/id #uuid "6296fb51-a261-5315-98e2-bafc87eb4fd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4d360a8-fe79-5362-9972-fed2a1994303" :question/math-academy-id "q-114074" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd84a82-8cbc-585f-8bbe-ce19fdb09a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247954} {:answer/id #uuid "47871075-deb3-513b-8a8e-3639234f622c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248060} {:answer/id #uuid "983ebb92-bd83-5ed1-a0f3-8fe2c8c188ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248782} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c31917-04d7-582e-b1d4-e26865d402a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248917} {:answer/id #uuid "af0b67fe-7271-56c8-8367-495b25ff2f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c31917-04d7-582e-b1d4-e26865d402a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248917} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f9281c-e5d7-5f72-ac5c-0b25153c48f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249738}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8425d47-32c7-547c-ab87-ac1c6071e1e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114078" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/8)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012323fc-4e7b-5948-bd33-ac6535cdacea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247423} {:answer/id #uuid "275108dc-ba21-516f-8c42-bd8bf8d71064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247772} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab5218b-e36e-59ff-8b03-f71a3f5c4374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247944} {:answer/id #uuid "82b6c265-2f3d-5dbe-b622-87847517b9ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248580} {:answer/id #uuid "afcf5a5d-6b1c-5e07-b91a-41eca607a863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcf5a5d-6b1c-5e07-b91a-41eca607a863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249002} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f84de4-1a81-5ce2-ac8e-5901c4a2a352" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c216ad6d-32f4-5235-ae6f-6f4e1e6db054" :question/math-academy-id "q-114080" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b573ef-1007-53ad-a1f4-f1bbb6a97f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247434} {:answer/id #uuid "21345a50-5601-54ac-b6b8-8854f3bcf25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247719} {:answer/id #uuid "21932059-2779-56bb-aff8-46d2133806aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247722} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ca1c00-7abb-53af-b061-a218e5f95af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249025} {:answer/id #uuid "fe379fad-f57a-50e1-ad28-7deffbfbf656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b573ef-1007-53ad-a1f4-f1bbb6a97f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247434} :answer-field/id #uuid "20529d1c-5c66-5379-87b8-bf5bcb3ca23c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249730}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d206bd2a-2b8b-589e-945a-46c1dd7ed6d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114084" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07df5620-8117-5d74-b65a-568506c2ddda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284848} {:answer/id #uuid "4699fac1-5a8f-5b40-afed-7064158b1c33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285437} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce9442e-a29f-597e-b2de-7761a1d30d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286222} {:answer/id #uuid "a22f372f-9504-584b-bc3e-87c16eaabc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286274} {:answer/id #uuid "e584a0a9-3825-5a55-8fc4-911388ec2a92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a22f372f-9504-584b-bc3e-87c16eaabc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286274} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ff436e5-f03c-513f-b406-812caeb45b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287249}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25b26ce0-b29c-55b2-a912-d3113c434dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-19393" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/16)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bbb1cae-6e39-530c-8350-eb936f667815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284882} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee39338-b490-52d5-8051-37da3e5e957f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285657} {:answer/id #uuid "64faa062-9068-565a-bb31-39dbd6d07913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285705} {:answer/id #uuid "68959faf-15c8-528e-bc75-90d2d2a0e5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285749} {:answer/id #uuid "f7445989-6f9b-5004-8c4b-e95fea2ee953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68959faf-15c8-528e-bc75-90d2d2a0e5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285749} :answer-field/id #uuid "77436f8b-d0d6-52c6-99f0-ade76c2dfb27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287399}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20d8d0f4-d57e-564e-be24-7116faf35cef" :question/math-academy-id "q-19395" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-12{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-12{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3\\cdot (1-4{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(2x)}^{2}.$   \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-0.5$ | $0.5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-12{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-0.5}^{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.5)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "331c449c-78bb-5f8b-9dcd-69e5f627c3c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285253} {:answer/id #uuid "53cbca06-5dff-57fe-91ef-daa24c5147f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285559} {:answer/id #uuid "7d34e51c-e8eb-58a3-86e7-2325ea4401f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285940} {:answer/id #uuid "c0230150-a2bf-5bf4-a26a-c06c4bd66ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286545} {:answer/id #uuid "db135799-7845-5945-af89-06c54826a98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0230150-a2bf-5bf4-a26a-c06c4bd66ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286545} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6de2d23-7e6a-5191-bba5-d88af28f962e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287530}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d25ee70-cfd4-55fa-9b35-c615d86700ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-19396" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can write this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $25{x}^{2}=(5x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319103 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e406c8b4-fe2c-53cd-abdc-dc32a0608267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e406c8b4-fe2c-53cd-abdc-dc32a0608267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318327} :answer-field/id #uuid "c443a9b7-8c24-5662-be21-7a311e519118" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318847}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ba9633b-5871-51f9-8aee-a3691915151d" :question/math-academy-id "q-346451" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{1}{1+(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a18383d3-63cd-5639-931d-a7a1c504ecad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a18383d3-63cd-5639-931d-a7a1c504ecad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318118} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4db02f7-5977-595a-8560-ebd6520e3bc1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318876}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "684a7fc3-f685-5be8-90e1-52ef15ddd822" :question/math-academy-id "q-346458" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/100)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{10}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/100}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/10)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{10})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{10}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{10}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=10\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/10)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7bafaa-3cbb-533d-b844-15cf79b3fe34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{5}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a7bafaa-3cbb-533d-b844-15cf79b3fe34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{5}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319530} :answer-field/id #uuid "f18bc040-ce10-594f-bb02-f617ff11efb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320672}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b439af01-6063-5a0d-8dfc-d235cf8c0346" :question/math-academy-id "q-351291" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5(1-16{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine, \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(4x)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{5}}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6d4b36a-43a6-585a-a12c-95ad82f0ab96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6d4b36a-43a6-585a-a12c-95ad82f0ab96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319889} :answer-field/id #uuid "1307c487-f3d6-5566-a68c-5623882801fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320199}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0098fa7-60fc-5090-aeb3-d82239a596c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-351827" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =15{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/36)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/36}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =5\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d6374a-a8f4-5012-ba14-79979bb09a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d6374a-a8f4-5012-ba14-79979bb09a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319994} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e46496-0573-5f7f-b6a6-15d10b4e8306" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320599}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "88256796-f1d7-5511-b30e-ef033cdfdfae" :question/math-academy-id "q-351834" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3\\cdot (1-25{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(5x)}^{2}.$   \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a220c465-cd23-556a-b6f2-70e7e4ee705c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a220c465-cd23-556a-b6f2-70e7e4ee705c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319874} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f065e5b-1a3e-5164-964f-ea2efbce87b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320306}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a43d62d-e653-5802-9217-17e3b89ace8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-351835" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(6x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{18}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320919 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ef55d3a-1d64-5e75-a936-57964a2c5268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ef55d3a-1d64-5e75-a936-57964a2c5268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319675} :answer-field/id #uuid "c611600a-1f7e-5aff-a691-ea5100dd312b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a866bed5-d733-533a-9199-2b822335e2cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a866bed5-d733-533a-9199-2b822335e2cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319897} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf733acb-7ff6-5434-afab-1202dfb73dee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320598}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "474d3d58-1cc2-50c1-8314-228946c22d89" :question/math-academy-id "q-351839" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{12}{3+27{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{12}{3+27{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=4{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $12$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{12}{3+27{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{1+(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{12}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{12}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(12)-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,arctan\\,(12)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e28a0da-0d28-58b0-9ea9-a556621c9cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e28a0da-0d28-58b0-9ea9-a556621c9cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319579} :answer-field/id #uuid "f17d058d-f41c-502a-aa59-824f88279a31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320671}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c01a93a-0fc6-5d70-b6e3-096c747b914e" :question/math-academy-id "q-351855" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡($\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/12)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/12}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{12})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{12}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{12}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{12})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d0c2f0-e1ef-5f9d-b277-1d69053a1f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330265} {:answer/id #uuid "5d04e998-1dc4-5619-8be2-aa1e5c1b7c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330779} {:answer/id #uuid "866ac174-f329-56ce-b375-426c38e8089c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331143} {:answer/id #uuid "a72e2a87-1718-5692-ae75-612ad60536bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331438} {:answer/id #uuid "d944c1b0-1445-5a57-b346-1c4580f6e918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a72e2a87-1718-5692-ae75-612ad60536bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331438} :answer-field/id #uuid "7066a7e5-a4e7-571e-8102-812757ff24f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332406}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf21744c-e558-571b-b3ed-9b3f13019f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-49538" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{1+(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e86a4b-cc4c-5a6f-aaf3-ef2234d941ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330588} {:answer/id #uuid "569e6b60-bf68-55c0-a58d-f5683e2d1476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330724} {:answer/id #uuid "87600d1e-7d95-5096-a855-c3bc9ca0e904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331159} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6b1507-21a9-5241-8a35-d41f437e8d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331368} {:answer/id #uuid "b73d0144-5e6d-5adf-89c2-88b202a8b0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b73d0144-5e6d-5adf-89c2-88b202a8b0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331568} :answer-field/id #uuid "ece6c44b-e4c3-57ea-8f7c-8273c4e5c5c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332617}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edefe020-e961-5a43-95be-73f3210a7870" :question/math-academy-id "q-49546" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\, & ={\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/25)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/25}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65f4d436-59f3-5763-bcdc-b3dd57872260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65f4d436-59f3-5763-bcdc-b3dd57872260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368430} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6eaf7b2-0903-5d1f-bf6c-e8f7966021aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29fd1abb-98ff-5074-9886-b94701e8a3c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29fd1abb-98ff-5074-9886-b94701e8a3c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368432} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef16f665-49b9-5951-8bf5-581178032400" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368431}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3aa951d0-f5d2-580d-8cda-935baa717731" :question/math-academy-id "q-351850" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/25)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,arctan\\,(5)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90c6aca-5f52-581d-b9b7-53525c39db0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377540} {:answer/id #uuid "35bc1324-3515-5f3b-b9da-7c903cdfb324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35bc1324-3515-5f3b-b9da-7c903cdfb324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427994} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d0f7cff-e86b-56b3-9a00-cbb02d98343e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377539}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4068a5d2-2d7d-5115-9e90-ed45feea5f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-351845" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/9)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{10}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15391250-e023-5a04-9057-9658fe4de707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427993} {:answer/id #uuid "83a4d996-c213-5d67-946a-4cd6fe97edb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427998} {:answer/id #uuid "abc0b7d1-6dfb-5790-a262-2aa331de3a0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427999} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2aeebc-c3cc-5f32-bec9-7d9027991243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428000} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5fd737-b612-553b-8e19-91de7f399fb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15391250-e023-5a04-9057-9658fe4de707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427993} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae824470-993a-5443-bdc9-a07993674d20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428005}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bacbcea3-6ad6-5840-9bf7-1e8371e0974d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114075" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/9)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/9}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Definite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Trigonometric Functions"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064093 :question/id #uuid "15473603-5bb5-5a20-8fc9-e4d7589ccb38" :question/math-academy-id "e-473" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048777 :topic/math-academy-id 285 :topic/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048867 :topic/math-academy-id 203 :topic/title "Simplifying Expressions Using Basic Trigonometric Identities"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c52f2bd-23e1-5bbd-91b0-10df3c8d5bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330057} {:answer/id #uuid "d36e0353-3583-56a8-bf43-9f9e46e158b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331823} {:answer/id #uuid "e7cfd460-df1c-5724-9a8c-2b87c5f96b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331983} {:answer/id #uuid "eac7a79e-f967-5990-8f18-a2ab6d8ca3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c52f2bd-23e1-5bbd-91b0-10df3c8d5bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330057} :answer-field/id #uuid "7aa9d753-56af-5317-ae24-c3f3f3d9c9be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332423}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8beed7b3-f15a-500c-aa6e-e151d8a3ea87" :question/math-academy-id "q-49070" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eef9722-f326-5995-94aa-696c6de0feb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431077} {:answer/id #uuid "ab45b025-5861-5024-8958-4ef3403a84cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431080} {:answer/id #uuid "c9711a7d-8c7c-54ef-b29c-11352c7fb2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431087} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6108cc-2a4c-50ea-9d2d-80ef3ef54486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431088} {:answer/id #uuid "f002d208-93d4-565e-847d-55497116f0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f002d208-93d4-565e-847d-55497116f0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431094} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd13680e-c437-5191-a0b8-f472cae34b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063198}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4246a553-248d-558d-9e27-dac3cd88b439" :question/math-academy-id "q-49271" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cot}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity ${cot}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cot}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3878ae79-1e5e-59bf-8bb6-ae0cf3aaa4bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247928} {:answer/id #uuid "5f75b493-3947-527e-a588-60cab80d2be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248287} {:answer/id #uuid "74e4c221-78c2-5702-af4f-442e99facd40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248451} {:answer/id #uuid "cef45258-9cb1-562e-a7e4-faf62bbc7406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249259} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dd153a-e09b-5898-9188-70f04b5e8044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3878ae79-1e5e-59bf-8bb6-ae0cf3aaa4bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247928} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b71088-363e-519b-b126-45df5c59e3e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250039}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40079a0f-e072-5ffd-a039-30e177ed76fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114304" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f3787c-03fd-50e2-8322-14d8ecbf8e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3f3787c-03fd-50e2-8322-14d8ecbf8e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319992} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5c16599-fe4a-59ff-9a06-18aea9c5678d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320577}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff9f5fe1-b925-5646-a0bd-3096b5a14063" :question/math-academy-id "q-352491" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}8\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity  $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}8\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=5x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=5x.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{\\pi }{15}$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u){|}_{-\\pi /3}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡0-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)-\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(1-0)-\\frac{8}{5}(2+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ee9771-ae2f-5017-8849-fca18997c0b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55ee9771-ae2f-5017-8849-fca18997c0b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319642} :answer-field/id #uuid "db5f7dac-82d7-59ef-94d1-d265197465de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320618}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f7dd2b0-51b1-5d08-9b2a-990f6402e6c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-352703" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x. \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "133f241b-3239-51ab-a093-dc6cccc2b3b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "133f241b-3239-51ab-a093-dc6cccc2b3b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319445} :answer-field/id #uuid "11de1101-33f9-5dca-9dfb-db14736527f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320196}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f0089c9-3669-540d-b79e-df09b425d3d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-352708" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(2-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(2-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(2-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15653369-8087-58f2-a8e7-ee1f42d7bd1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15653369-8087-58f2-a8e7-ee1f42d7bd1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319451} :answer-field/id #uuid "9db4e630-3874-5b54-aff1-bc86595d9e47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320481}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "000ae74d-dd6f-5b32-9992-57c0820ccae9" :question/math-academy-id "q-352710" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(3-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(3\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00252c74-e799-5912-972c-eafc461625e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329952} {:answer/id #uuid "3223b1cf-b4b2-565a-8efe-e52a96ee4dd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330390} {:answer/id #uuid "4263076a-2503-5230-8400-61f62c8e0d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330544} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1e19f8-9d06-53c8-981c-08e4b8b37875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331035} {:answer/id #uuid "f171d783-ddda-55c0-8a43-adf76df06c3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3223b1cf-b4b2-565a-8efe-e52a96ee4dd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330390} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf41caff-7c0c-5479-97f5-98d355acd89f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df3aa7c1-38d6-5ddf-a732-477c8eceab1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49258" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b7cf8f-bcce-5eb2-9e2b-d634b7d1d4f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330099} {:answer/id #uuid "12b7179f-1b92-5e99-a7b9-29de6e25a71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330109} {:answer/id #uuid "9ed74260-8967-54c8-a982-79627134f8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331374} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e94cb7-1494-5d46-b1b3-78ae25482c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331719} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e590e3-3337-590b-a068-6ead06d74561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10b7cf8f-bcce-5eb2-9e2b-d634b7d1d4f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330099} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac043f6d-7a72-52c6-9ca4-b976607baf36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332501}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b31b1059-0bef-5971-a208-8d252626b22e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49272" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc5237a-c69b-55ae-b866-010d3f7a5bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330371} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd1cdcd-2921-5ddc-b909-e7e993685c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330489} {:answer/id #uuid "50fef89f-04e0-57c1-8ae4-fc0b3a91c400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330683} {:answer/id #uuid "8245d36a-a259-5c47-8ea5-6c5ffebba5d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331100} {:answer/id #uuid "912e4360-a6f3-5690-971b-e8aa27cc95d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8245d36a-a259-5c47-8ea5-6c5ffebba5d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331100} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e525583-0340-50af-b1e3-515ea118e8bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332244}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c28e3047-44ec-5cae-a521-e1a19c0409df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49274" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d794c3d-0f93-5e9b-859b-c340a6282610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330206} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2fc078-2b62-5d65-868e-79b45fc7931e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330500} {:answer/id #uuid "43112ebc-3e8a-5866-aa5d-6e50c43cc18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330551} {:answer/id #uuid "d79174d3-f14b-59a5-9d4a-8261c63a8d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331855} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6ec74e-8319-5846-b8a1-18ee324765f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d79174d3-f14b-59a5-9d4a-8261c63a8d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331855} :answer-field/id #uuid "711e8728-f052-51b4-a0b9-2a8ed9eb7bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332407}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54f3f214-d6dd-5486-9655-fb3920d2f817" :question/math-academy-id "q-51109" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡2x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡u}{2}{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250b85cf-f9d6-591c-929e-2bd040932967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431062} {:answer/id #uuid "509e529a-c315-525e-8dd6-81ff51ba0502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431068} {:answer/id #uuid "63d630c2-d867-5897-a83c-5179a2334d2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431069} {:answer/id #uuid "d2651229-f5ff-524e-ae48-22a82959fa2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431089} {:answer/id #uuid "f748e060-6e5e-5da9-b6ea-84a0653e22cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "509e529a-c315-525e-8dd6-81ff51ba0502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431068} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec74a8fe-dc16-5d8a-9024-ad8266707d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c4f53f7-a91f-5a87-b60c-2cd20463d6e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114301" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4783ae01-0409-5f42-a49a-a5011eafe80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4783ae01-0409-5f42-a49a-a5011eafe80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431065} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8cb6fe3-1966-59eb-9541-67fe64eb26b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdc94a5e-ffa3-5e3c-b067-8b7e71e5c799" :question/math-academy-id "q-358219" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}3\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}3\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-sin\\,(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a74f3d-6597-59e4-b81c-8406532b8b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86a74f3d-6597-59e4-b81c-8406532b8b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431076} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a251513-9691-50f6-b973-f2685262f1ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431100}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d54d59da-aeb4-5592-b790-f9a9feee5b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-358220" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}\\frac{9}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}\\frac{9}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}9{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}9{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}9{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{3}-1) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064094 :question/id #uuid "68d2eb66-87ab-5182-9669-376bd1f70673" :question/math-academy-id "e-474" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3541e9d4-b110-5c63-a736-7fc7f4d31791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330422} {:answer/id #uuid "86df8515-e1e9-50e5-8ffa-c0f477c898b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331153} {:answer/id #uuid "9dec32d8-d9c0-5660-8378-5288983a6ac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331364} {:answer/id #uuid "a3922fe0-a979-577b-8dba-fd55ff68e732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331416} {:answer/id #uuid "f1373522-1826-5a96-a8aa-2b1480b28e0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86df8515-e1e9-50e5-8ffa-c0f477c898b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331153} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc984231-74ce-5ee3-a0d9-26f2e71c9fc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332589}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c589cab7-d081-524b-ae47-ab787d74dcb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-49273" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that ${cot}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16897289-4603-55b3-85a9-7a4e51b12fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330138} {:answer/id #uuid "351bd75d-098f-5b2a-b526-a98d2a025590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330419} {:answer/id #uuid "50b59dc3-9cc4-5d56-8dae-d5fde6823b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{tan}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330681} {:answer/id #uuid "9532f3f6-9b3e-5893-931d-79b72c8db1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{csc}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331272} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8968e8-f099-5f73-8828-0a36b59f6c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc8968e8-f099-5f73-8828-0a36b59f6c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331612} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b7347c5-9c24-53ba-ae9d-867009e5aca2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332398}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f71f24a-4751-5945-a98f-4a541dbf6232" :question/math-academy-id "q-49275" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d87cf2-ba4e-5ee2-b888-16334d204447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247661} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfa8fa7-c8a9-5491-a85f-a85434d1131e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247678} {:answer/id #uuid "5b42bf75-0d9b-5855-aac9-9999790d5338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248251} {:answer/id #uuid "a03cb483-a296-5946-8a8d-952eac55cad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248855} {:answer/id #uuid "aedb9126-7c6d-5c55-ad4b-869a319638e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d87cf2-ba4e-5ee2-b888-16334d204447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247661} :answer-field/id #uuid "0416b7bd-da37-58c6-8855-48ba00ca405e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249671}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edc6fd62-64ca-5ae7-b219-55728bf85a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114306" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2621a51d-6ea2-5c0c-b0e8-ef9a5309fa09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247760} {:answer/id #uuid "679c8c73-db45-58a5-8311-c18d1aa796b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248353} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bb94e3-7ab2-5067-a9f7-907364396e08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248924} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6ee47a-69b2-58b2-804c-4404e96412f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249242} {:answer/id #uuid "e05fabc1-bec3-5016-a5ff-3dafd2caba5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "679c8c73-db45-58a5-8311-c18d1aa796b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248353} :answer-field/id #uuid "580bbc55-c5cf-5ded-aa0f-fb666956d730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249830}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6eaf6d0-3cca-5bcd-87e4-c38716de9570" :question/math-academy-id "q-114313" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} {:answer/id #uuid "6f81ffd7-1892-5f9b-9320-925504438589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248407} {:answer/id #uuid "89d313a8-f000-577f-a816-a34a6622496f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248650} {:answer/id #uuid "a7092c76-1bc1-50c0-b6c7-d05f207eda48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248909} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f08285-93fd-5b63-ade9-e4f908688cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1b567b-6514-5d16-ba8c-83023f80f2da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249806}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "062977fc-037b-5a67-9a07-c0d038a63f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114318" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-[1-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321044 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "462d7b89-af8a-5c2e-b805-e15614972827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "462d7b89-af8a-5c2e-b805-e15614972827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319600} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa61f05-88d7-5c7e-bfdb-5df86d383bfb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320228}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af52ce4e-f719-5000-b6c3-23ef65c6c7c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-352848" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$  and  $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b25d05e-a29c-5b3e-80ba-83d6aca552d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b25d05e-a29c-5b3e-80ba-83d6aca552d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319807} :answer-field/id #uuid "1884c79a-7c8a-55aa-8077-27787e875e2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320220}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b97a69d0-fbb0-59ef-94ce-c6ff4a9fe97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352853" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$  and  $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})-(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b125d5a-83ca-5e84-9c6c-1590eeef63a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b125d5a-83ca-5e84-9c6c-1590eeef63a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319660} :answer-field/id #uuid "33891e7d-5b36-5ffb-bf17-86c9a9e0a09e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320286}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32053bdd-3d3f-5ab1-835c-4a43eb611286" :question/math-academy-id "q-352858" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-sin\\,(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa67265c-58c2-5525-a76e-07d76e4d6c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa67265c-58c2-5525-a76e-07d76e4d6c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319907} :answer-field/id #uuid "2de44fcf-9a78-5bd7-9b48-93e1a12d9e69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320270}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6cc98cbb-1926-5fbd-b202-06c3cb8a795d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352867" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=5x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=5x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75781285-f568-5213-b859-431f02aade49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75781285-f568-5213-b859-431f02aade49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319746} :answer-field/id #uuid "c391ebff-e18b-5edc-94f9-bf83e99d6410" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320569}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c92829c-a2f6-56f6-ab9b-8cc246269a34" :question/math-academy-id "q-352868" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b77ad6-2790-5fb9-ac75-c531ab004c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330601} {:answer/id #uuid "8a571c79-fa20-5257-bd99-b3a3310b2bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331178} {:answer/id #uuid "8b31c3cf-dd75-5df7-9b83-aa025a1ed598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331185} {:answer/id #uuid "9549f7ba-8509-55bb-ac17-34f5f78e130c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331274} {:answer/id #uuid "d75920df-cc3f-5f99-8620-29d4802abe07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48b77ad6-2790-5fb9-ac75-c531ab004c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330601} :answer-field/id #uuid "075617b4-7fd7-5fe0-bba2-6157b32a856f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332206}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a78f750a-573a-57da-b09b-e012074904df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49284" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e77e606-3fbe-52e7-aab0-b4caa65a952e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339394} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1abc9f-f1fd-5412-8a4f-d3cc8ce84141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339400} {:answer/id #uuid "4b46d088-8900-59df-a294-e9c5fdb831c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339803} {:answer/id #uuid "caf8e344-d78b-5248-b740-b9b631236223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340926} {:answer/id #uuid "dbec64d1-1c16-522f-a4e9-422136eadbca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f1abc9f-f1fd-5412-8a4f-d3cc8ce84141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339400} :answer-field/id #uuid "934751e0-e49e-590a-9aa0-5f8c7d1fc3cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341639}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47640681-1f63-58a5-b2bd-140af66b43bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73361" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58575d51-ffdd-543a-bade-6634febbdd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{cot}^{2}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339934} {:answer/id #uuid "7a186c20-1506-5364-98fb-f5f5b90eafc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340219} {:answer/id #uuid "a09f4f00-858f-53bb-8ec8-28c387d75743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340585} {:answer/id #uuid "b49ad4dc-2081-5be8-ae64-74edb3e4c85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{csc}^{2}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340766} {:answer/id #uuid "d84932da-0d02-599c-86d1-0c8975757cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a09f4f00-858f-53bb-8ec8-28c387d75743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340585} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2214d64-85df-5343-8f56-2f58cd99796e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341750}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6ad08b6-febc-5a5b-8528-78fb972c420b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74279" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{{sin}^{2}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{{sin}^{2}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡4x\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡4x\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26c30e3f-d29e-5013-9514-d17c3eee3460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339466} {:answer/id #uuid "376779f8-ab66-595c-9bd0-478fd63c0239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339625} {:answer/id #uuid "447b1d64-6d6b-508d-818e-c81c4fc983e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339733} {:answer/id #uuid "744da144-5af4-5254-8514-317a1d8d743d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340164} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6a59f6-df8c-5517-879f-5849fb7de659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26c30e3f-d29e-5013-9514-d17c3eee3460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339466} :answer-field/id #uuid "ede24e4d-4785-5cd1-8533-d9afadca7785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341806}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "504ab9d3-58bf-5555-aee6-cd8fa47fea51" :question/math-academy-id "q-74281" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int (1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int (\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce83bb5-48a8-5755-a136-3a2157d2ef78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431057} {:answer/id #uuid "854da0b1-b538-5abb-9128-538e7a7c49e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431075} {:answer/id #uuid "bb236701-7224-5bb8-9211-7b2730f8e9b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431083} {:answer/id #uuid "c6086863-df11-58f0-9fa7-5134443d4b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431085} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6b0533-0ce9-53e9-9ea2-abb22d26246a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6086863-df11-58f0-9fa7-5134443d4b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431085} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca77544-0046-5524-9cef-1c8e548a94a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431105}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a4cd24e-1cbf-547b-aab3-c78dc742ec94" :question/math-academy-id "q-114308" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}({tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that ${tan}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ade44e9-b6f9-500e-bc09-791aec3c4112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431063} {:answer/id #uuid "6590c99b-1fe0-54a5-9f86-8aebcedc658b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431071} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4d7986-64b5-5587-b804-bab2a0930585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431072} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2dad62-d368-5197-b93b-e3e45fe17653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431081} {:answer/id #uuid "fd953cc5-abf5-5b0c-84f3-3e4672a326d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6590c99b-1fe0-54a5-9f86-8aebcedc658b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431071} :answer-field/id #uuid "e803221b-b806-5450-a5a1-2379c91d357f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431108}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49b73c78-3335-57b5-a631-c7f8dd771090" :question/math-academy-id "q-73365" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1161462-0f9d-545a-a5a5-27e6a35427ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1161462-0f9d-545a-a5a5-27e6a35427ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431092} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe9e96d-c290-5de0-aea5-06fc2a18c7e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431102}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77e54e57-de69-5688-a9c9-dfe71c2ce5e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-352711" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b90dc2-4752-56a7-9b8f-d500c9d40dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431054} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc5523c-58ee-55e0-80dd-791ed4446cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431059} {:answer/id #uuid "a842be8e-7dd8-5330-8aa6-c7e1963f7629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431079} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c701b6-77f3-5b86-8e8d-cbfebc97a0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431084} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc2a33e-12cb-5317-9535-02af0caa9a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffc2a33e-12cb-5317-9535-02af0caa9a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431098} :answer-field/id #uuid "07a0cda5-2de4-5cc2-802a-a5549d6da26a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431099}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cd683e0-e43d-570b-a907-b426c76c1c6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114319" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =-[\\frac{1}{2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57752369-ee0f-585d-9307-31648dc6aed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505282} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf67a66-1f7d-589b-9794-976a6ee03856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505324} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6725ad-f38e-5393-96b7-7603ac0c2f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505329} {:answer/id #uuid "a9187687-7c45-54ed-92e1-7d05ac532cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505442} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f34fb5-2b1a-527d-8cbd-18a361eec573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f34fb5-2b1a-527d-8cbd-18a361eec573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505455} :answer-field/id #uuid "9163b72a-ca3f-56d5-be84-6c361f7f2037" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505673}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bcf19778-fecb-5e86-ab67-3237ac262859" :question/math-academy-id "q-73357" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡3x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡3x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ | $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064095 :question/id #uuid "b34db891-0676-505c-9ba3-57d86f1d9b94" :question/math-academy-id "e-475" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050489 :topic/math-academy-id 478 :topic/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d293006-4557-52f7-97fa-89b713f04bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290961} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab6bfaa-7ece-5e67-90de-208a2d4feb0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291089} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc46aa2-9ded-556b-a537-a1a679cb6433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291165} {:answer/id #uuid "eebf6cc8-3213-5f0c-a405-dc3bb9ec335f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291631} {:answer/id #uuid "f4175e71-0599-5150-8c8c-aa81a58e1f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4175e71-0599-5150-8c8c-aa81a58e1f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291660} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58655bb-396e-5e05-9eb3-4ff0743264b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292503}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1fabab33-132f-500c-992f-45cbf132915e" :question/math-academy-id "q-2622" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1953b710-b82c-577e-98b6-790ad3f6376f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330165} {:answer/id #uuid "47a09229-1f79-52b7-a980-e0b91c222810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330595} {:answer/id #uuid "5f05a2ca-3546-5073-8f36-2d0892a8d2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330795} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3a6511-5653-5a35-b752-9a75fb78b8d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331041} {:answer/id #uuid "dfdb4294-e4cf-53fe-b9e6-7df714f3b303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfdb4294-e4cf-53fe-b9e6-7df714f3b303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331926} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd1cb44-ea37-542f-889e-7a707a092e16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eeffd6d0-ba71-5af0-8a18-c001ad19ba1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49259" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} {:answer/id #uuid "7229d8df-ae59-5660-b41e-cae11851e04c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248420} {:answer/id #uuid "91224b99-89c4-59ce-b789-19a10d61178d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248714} {:answer/id #uuid "dc01fc34-a583-577b-8fdc-401ef22073b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249369} {:answer/id #uuid "f20a32cf-99d1-5344-b1f0-7a8da3242cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec890aa8-f649-5040-b0db-08c864882cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250082}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de415510-24b2-53a0-b8c3-ddc9cdee62b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114294" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{3}⁡x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40aa56b-ab70-5e10-858c-cf521e2db7ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b40aa56b-ab70-5e10-858c-cf521e2db7ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318173} :answer-field/id #uuid "b308216d-b811-5250-bc3b-cb96f7740d70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318809}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0a9ebacf-0ee8-5c1e-ba6d-9dd55f05b2b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-347941" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da4ca77e-eea8-594f-9d7a-670f98ed3e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da4ca77e-eea8-594f-9d7a-670f98ed3e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320057} :answer-field/id #uuid "313bd619-a7ad-546a-8a4d-49815332682f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320277}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "313e0a29-ace7-5c0c-a6d4-e0a9a2fe5bcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-352786" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{3}\\,x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{3}\\,x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}\\,x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c4c17b5-6041-5b4a-921e-16d5b13a2a5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319573} {:answer/id #uuid "da2d4300-1fc2-5499-8622-53086d327657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da2d4300-1fc2-5499-8622-53086d327657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431090} :answer-field/id #uuid "786408a1-4911-5c78-8041-0f51f924f24b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "00fe6411-9f3d-58f9-a531-7305d81e2e57" :question/math-academy-id "q-352797" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6757c155-e294-52b7-8fb8-597465763d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}(3)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6757c155-e294-52b7-8fb8-597465763d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}(3)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319707} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4172f40-bc38-5518-9248-9fb66fd19962" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320680}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "07713ce3-1f95-5769-81d0-a1d74de4220e" :question/math-academy-id "q-352798" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93e3e9f0-e68a-5543-83f9-3acf9772a970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93e3e9f0-e68a-5543-83f9-3acf9772a970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322323} :answer-field/id #uuid "77e733a9-1d70-5175-b37a-21480c860c60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323404}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a618cdf1-860e-5928-99cb-d500520f67b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-362157" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}{|}_{1}^{1/2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83244f3f-d4c0-5400-b575-23be5005ae8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331114} {:answer/id #uuid "af9bdfa5-e153-5f0e-9579-128cbb842449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{2}⁡3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331502} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b54574-c597-5d2e-b623-f716b57a4a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332087} {:answer/id #uuid "faa172fc-7c4f-5556-9b0f-aa9ceeebb1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332150} {:answer/id #uuid "fbfd483a-4f6a-531f-b6bb-82a660adeb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbfd483a-4f6a-531f-b6bb-82a660adeb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332164} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d0ff93-0be5-5775-8d8d-a9a9d7becf1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80f918c1-b02c-51df-b3e3-2c8413bacd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-49256" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10304a96-adfd-5511-8b38-70b4e4cb2215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330091} {:answer/id #uuid "6da2efe0-b31d-592f-96a9-1b37aaf477e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330932} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e3fa5a-567a-51e0-bc36-1958095f5813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331682} {:answer/id #uuid "dc447439-382c-515e-b293-790fca1f2316" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331901} {:answer/id #uuid "f47329b5-6d59-5ad4-b066-1dc0b16cbbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da2efe0-b31d-592f-96a9-1b37aaf477e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330932} :answer-field/id #uuid "70002cb7-bb15-57f9-b1f8-e67051228ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332405}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e2d21ac-046c-5274-bb89-c9bfaff5e9df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49257" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}{|}_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b95828-a685-54a8-96b4-b52ae657e912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330153} {:answer/id #uuid "444fa90c-41cd-594e-acf1-cfca43d9f868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330563} {:answer/id #uuid "4e61c48b-d79c-5d63-9602-758c8c834289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330664} {:answer/id #uuid "7f11ee4d-4f0b-51c9-8e3d-549f4a158d4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331072} {:answer/id #uuid "89b1ee96-afb9-5e02-a824-2992fac6b5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "444fa90c-41cd-594e-acf1-cfca43d9f868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330563} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f414d51-cc19-5057-95ed-395de2e5b540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332345}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3ad6824-baa3-5500-876c-87beb97cf8ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-49277" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}+C \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{-1}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24eeb023-368d-5caf-bde7-f9b11a6219a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡3x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330267} {:answer/id #uuid "36e74ac0-ccec-5862-8ba0-9d4f3e6809f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330443} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef8bdce-d78c-52be-8ab1-8b4ea707f2d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331215} {:answer/id #uuid "9f71f3e9-0996-5cad-9e0f-7742b4c0eda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331384} {:answer/id #uuid "c436875d-9186-5501-bd3a-54bdb18939af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f71f3e9-0996-5cad-9e0f-7742b4c0eda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331384} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9e35f53-e6a6-565d-a328-353c93f1466f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332525}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b48a93f-4b08-53d3-bef8-fd2388b47477" :question/math-academy-id "q-49278" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ab7134-266a-55b0-8dd9-092f7793e4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330457} {:answer/id #uuid "75ef0166-fd95-54fe-b5df-525ead63381c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331008} {:answer/id #uuid "95684c85-1b97-54e9-97fb-b17ebcc31860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331275} {:answer/id #uuid "d81e6757-4b9f-56b0-99e6-30d04faf2681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331866} {:answer/id #uuid "e3374bc6-ffec-53a1-9944-f67c29759f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{tan}^{2}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95684c85-1b97-54e9-97fb-b17ebcc31860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331275} :answer-field/id #uuid "89d8ab03-5e24-50d3-bb4c-13c096f28d48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332443}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73bdd419-9ea0-5251-ace5-0e2f286a0252" :question/math-academy-id "q-49280" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c5821ad-3d4f-57c6-a299-5d7eb8eb6393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330643} {:answer/id #uuid "9313388c-be46-561d-9054-618eddeb5792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331257} {:answer/id #uuid "968b5dbc-fc14-52e1-b8ba-c858af9d76e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331286} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf4b03b-f1c8-5d81-b6e3-2abcf9f93640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331617} {:answer/id #uuid "fd662dda-2335-5bcb-a678-23c74459f46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "968b5dbc-fc14-52e1-b8ba-c858af9d76e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331286} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ced3b9-575e-546e-8f36-c27932699fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332518}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c693f81-0fae-5be2-839f-6622073dd810" :question/math-academy-id "q-49281" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let  $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2015152c-6dd4-56e6-906d-eca5aee8113b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431060} {:answer/id #uuid "64b06414-fa24-5496-803e-0ac49b1edb16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431070} {:answer/id #uuid "8054347c-d721-5221-af8e-16ee957f8128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431073} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf286e8-c095-5023-811d-f2ea8779fe1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431078} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e9383f-e46d-5cc2-b821-2e62b2d63f2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bf286e8-c095-5023-811d-f2ea8779fe1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431078} :answer-field/id #uuid "92469112-1ed0-55aa-bae5-7ad7d5ef9904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a60367e9-cec6-56ff-bdf1-1a7368d63d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-10040" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)}\\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1| \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f4f35f-6fb8-5362-bb51-1c0b0c319dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431055} {:answer/id #uuid "14b36ff5-eeb9-52d4-b7b8-21c79368f8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431056} {:answer/id #uuid "41aaf43b-2c95-50cf-a8a3-79ae4c22104b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431064} {:answer/id #uuid "85271a33-9aae-5b9d-a3b8-a96dd470bdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431074} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaf3e71-8a60-5d8e-be80-97ff5b0a7a92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14b36ff5-eeb9-52d4-b7b8-21c79368f8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431056} :answer-field/id #uuid "82084fd2-bb79-5568-8b5b-a9fbb9530769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431103}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c26cdc41-d401-5858-96e0-ffa4a20294ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-49279" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,du={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\sqrt{3}}{u}^{2}\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({(\\sqrt{3})}^{3}-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(3\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(3-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{27}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4afbb947-1a46-57c3-a2dc-395ab6315772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4afbb947-1a46-57c3-a2dc-395ab6315772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431066} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c69fd7b-4aa9-5d3d-a2cf-a03772cdb2a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431101}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dadcc805-1744-58ea-b449-313016666d23" :question/math-academy-id "q-362158" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /24}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /24}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /24}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc34fbe-0ac6-5122-9d50-7ed8124d6804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431058} {:answer/id #uuid "229fc38f-7a75-5c2c-bdb9-4a89c232f57e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431061} {:answer/id #uuid "4e22d3f7-480b-5511-8fa6-2677b36f174d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431067} {:answer/id #uuid "c810647a-c42a-522a-8d4e-5301429d057c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431086} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7daa64-9324-5510-bf53-292b940a1d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fc34fbe-0ac6-5122-9d50-7ed8124d6804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431058} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27fa184-c2a1-506b-ac6d-5109a0a21c79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431107}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f01d9ac9-bb7d-5b0c-be19-2dc05bc65cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114295" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,⟹\\,-2\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc5eff9-4511-5ebc-9346-fef6d3ff2cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505293} {:answer/id #uuid "61a52828-b97a-55bc-89af-abdc326b7088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505301} {:answer/id #uuid "a747a90c-e5d0-5aef-9c1b-23569a104c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505440} {:answer/id #uuid "bf18c3df-1eff-5189-830c-ed12cf41dde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505476} {:answer/id #uuid "cae550b1-5979-52c8-970e-b1b797158855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a747a90c-e5d0-5aef-9c1b-23569a104c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505440} :answer-field/id #uuid "7876217b-a5c3-5d52-8219-aba955692660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505660}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b6577b4-d24d-5962-9f5c-436ba639df8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73371" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{4}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{4}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{4}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{5}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{5}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{u}^{-4}}{-4}){|}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}){|}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{1}{{1}^{4}}-{(\\frac{2}{1})}^{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(1-16) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5976a6b-1d1d-57ce-8564-63c89f695029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5976a6b-1d1d-57ce-8564-63c89f695029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505555} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5cb8799-b859-5b82-be20-c6134d8d1332" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505696}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e2444a41-f0c0-50e5-91b8-38bd6aeb8a43" :question/math-academy-id "q-347942" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{4}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡3x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{4}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{4}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{5}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{18}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /18}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{5}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{{u}^{-4}}{-4}){|}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}){|}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{1}{{1}^{4}}-{(\\frac{2}{1})}^{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}(1-16) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}]}
